{"id":85308,"docketId":2247673,"caseName":"The Atalanta.\u2014 Faussat","caseNameFull":"The Atalanta.-Faussat, Claimant","slug":"the-atalanta-faussat","docketNumber":"","dateFiled":"1820-03-17","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1820,"scdbId":"1820-027","direction":"Liberal","votesMajority":7,"votesMinority":0,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":"<p>A question of proprietary interest on farther proof. Condemnation pronounced.</p>","proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":1,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":85308,"type":"majority","typeCode":"010combined","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":753,"isHtml":true,"text":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<opinion data-order=\"3\" data-type=\"opinion\" id=\"x999-1\" type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"b443-8\">\n  This cause- was continued at February term, 1818,\n  <a class=\"footnote\" href=\"#fna\" id=\"fna_ref\">\n   a\n  </a>\n  for farther proof, but the farther proof received at the last term being unsatisfactory, it was again continued, on account of some peculiar circumstances in the case, to the presept term, when no farther proof being produced, condemnation was pronounced.\n </p>\n<p id=\"AKJ\">\n  Decree reversed.\n </p>\n\n<div class=\"footnotes\"><div class=\"footnote\" id=\"fna\" label=\"a\">\n<a class=\"footnote\" href=\"#fna_ref\">\n   a\n  </a>\n<p id=\"b443-10\">\n<em>\n    Vide Ante, Vol.\n   </em>\n   III. p. 409.\n  </p>\n</div></div></opinion>"}],"citations":[]}